## 📖 Overview

**CI/CD** is an important software development practice used to automate the process of **integrating, building, testing, and delivering applications**.

CI/CD helps developers identify problems earlier and release software more efficiently.

```text
CI/CD
 │
 ├── CI → Continuous Integration
 │
 └── CD → Continuous Delivery / Continuous Deployment
```

---

## 🔁 What is CI/CD?

CI/CD consists of:

|  Term  | Full Form              | Basic Purpose                           |
| :----: | :--------------------- | :-------------------------------------- |
| **CI** | Continuous Integration | Frequently integrate and test code      |
| **CD** | Continuous Delivery    | Keep software ready for deployment      |
| **CD** | Continuous Deployment  | Automatically deploy successful changes |

A basic CI/CD process looks like:

```text
Code
  ↓
Build
  ↓
Test
  ↓
Deploy
```

---

# 🔨 Continuous Integration (CI)

**Continuous Integration** is the practice of frequently integrating code changes into a shared repository.

Developers regularly push their changes:

```text
Developer A ──┐
              │
Developer B ──┼──► Git Repository
              │
Developer C ──┘
```

After new code is pushed, automated processes can build and test the application.

```text
Developer
    │
    │ Push Code
    ▼
Git Repository
    │
    ▼
   Build
    │
    ▼
   Test
    │
    ▼
  Result
```

---

## 💻 Simple CI Example

A developer makes changes and pushes them:

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Add new feature"
git push origin main
```

A CI system can then automatically:

1. Download the latest source code.
2. Build the application.
3. Run automated tests.
4. Report whether the process succeeded or failed.

---

## ✅ Benefits of Continuous Integration

| Benefit                     | Description                                |
| :-------------------------- | :----------------------------------------- |
| 🐛 **Early Bug Detection**  | Problems can be identified quickly         |
| 🧪 **Automated Testing**    | Tests can run automatically                |
| 🔨 **Automated Builds**     | Application builds can run automatically   |
| ⚡ **Quick Feedback**        | Developers receive faster results          |
| 🤝 **Better Collaboration** | Developers frequently integrate their work |

