# 📦 Continuous Delivery

**Continuous Delivery** extends Continuous Integration.

After the application is successfully built and tested, it is kept in a state where it is **ready for deployment**.

```text
Code
  ↓
Build
  ↓
Test
  ↓
Ready for Deployment
  ↓
Manual Approval
  ↓
Production
```

> 💡 **Simple Definition:**
> Continuous Delivery means that the application is **always ready to be deployed**, but the final production deployment may require manual approval.

---

# 🚀 Continuous Deployment

**Continuous Deployment** automatically releases changes after they successfully pass all required automated checks.

```text
Code
  ↓
Build
  ↓
Test
  ↓
Automatic Deployment
  ↓
Production
```

> 💡 **Simple Definition:**
> Continuous Deployment means that successfully tested changes can be **automatically deployed to production**.

---

## 🆚 Continuous Delivery vs Continuous Deployment

| Feature                    | Continuous Delivery | Continuous Deployment |
| :------------------------- | :-----------------: | :-------------------: |
| Automated Build            |          ✅          |           ✅           |
| Automated Testing          |          ✅          |           ✅           |
| Software Ready for Release |          ✅          |           ✅           |
| Production Deployment      |      Controlled     |       Automatic       |
| Manual Approval            |   Usually Required  |      Not Required     |

### Easy Way to Remember

```text
Continuous Delivery
        │
        ▼
   Ready to Deploy


Continuous Deployment
        │
        ▼
 Automatically Deployed
```

