# ⚙️ What is a CI/CD Pipeline?

A **CI/CD pipeline** is a sequence of automated steps that software goes through before being released.

A basic pipeline:

```text
┌─────────────┐
│    Code     │
└──────┬──────┘
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│    Build    │
└──────┬──────┘
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│    Test     │
└──────┬──────┘
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│   Deploy    │
└─────────────┘
```

---

## 📋 Basic Pipeline Stages

|     Stage     | Description                              |
| :-----------: | :--------------------------------------- |
|  💻 **Code**  | Developer writes or modifies source code |
|  📤 **Push**  | Code is pushed to the repository         |
|  🔨 **Build** | Application is compiled or packaged      |
|  🧪 **Test**  | Automated tests verify the application   |
| 🚀 **Deploy** | Successful application is released       |

---

# 🌿 Role of Git in CI/CD

Git repositories commonly act as the starting point for CI/CD pipelines.

```text
Developer
    │
    ▼
Write Code
    │
    ▼
Git Commit
    │
    ▼
Git Push
    │
    ▼
GitHub / GitLab
    │
    ▼
CI/CD Pipeline
```

A push to a repository can be configured to automatically trigger a CI/CD workflow.

---

# 🔨 Build Process

During the build stage, source code is converted into a usable application package.

For a Java Maven project:

```bash
mvn clean package
```

A successful build may generate a JAR file:

```text
target/
└── application.jar
```

---

# 🧪 Testing in CI/CD

Automated testing is an important part of a CI/CD pipeline.

If tests pass:

```text
Build
  │
  ▼
Tests Passed
  │
  ▼
Continue Pipeline
```

If tests fail:

```text
Build
  │
  ▼
Tests Failed
  │
  ▼
Stop Pipeline
  │
  ▼
Developer Fixes Issue
```

> 💡 Automated testing helps prevent incorrect code from progressing further through the delivery process.

---

# 🚀 Deployment

After successful build and testing, the application can be deployed.

A simple environment flow can be:

```text
Development
     │
     ▼
   Testing
     │
     ▼
   Staging
     │
     ▼
 Production
```

| Environment        | Purpose                         |
| :----------------- | :------------------------------ |
| 💻 **Development** | Application development         |
| 🧪 **Testing**     | Application verification        |
| 🎭 **Staging**     | Final testing before production |
| 🚀 **Production**  | Live application for users      |

