# 📚 Important CI/CD Terms

| Term           | Meaning                                                 |
| :------------- | :------------------------------------------------------ |
| **CI**         | Continuous Integration                                  |
| **CD**         | Continuous Delivery / Continuous Deployment             |
| **Pipeline**   | Automated sequence of build, test, and deployment steps |
| **Build**      | Process of preparing source code for execution          |
| **Test**       | Verification that application behavior is correct       |
| **Artifact**   | Output produced by the build process                    |
| **Deploy**     | Release application to an environment                   |
| **Production** | Live environment used by end users                      |
| **Automation** | Performing processes automatically                      |

---

# 🆚 Manual Process vs CI/CD

| Manual Process                   | CI/CD Process               |
| :------------------------------- | :-------------------------- |
| Build performed manually         | Build can be automated      |
| Tests may be executed manually   | Tests can run automatically |
| Slow feedback                    | Faster feedback             |
| More repetitive work             | Reduced repetitive work     |
| Deployment may take longer       | Deployment can be faster    |
| Higher chance of manual mistakes | More consistent process     |

